# tests/llm-call, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST, of a worker. Nothing here was ever about the client: the
# subject is the HTTP request std/llm-call builds and the text it extracts from
# the reply, and the stub is the mock that observes both. The client was
# carried for one reason — a secret store is built client-side — and that is
# now injected by caos-tools/test, which grants std/llm-call a mock key on the
# dev stack for the whole suite.
#
# `--llm-call:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-call` and `--stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --relay:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/relay.sh` hand this
# worker the BUILT artifacts: naming a dependency with `:@=` EVALUATES it, so a
# worker never has to (its caos has eval-path-then and no eval-path).
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --llm-call:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-call --stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --relay:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/relay.sh
